@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+---
+type: implementation
+status: verified
+owner: codex-reservation-expiry
+feature_ledger: cascade:reservation-expiry
+created_at: 2026-09-29
+related_paths: [src/cascade/client/base.py, src/cascade/client/execution.py, src/cascade/client/query.py, src/cascade/replay.py]
+truth_sources: [code, user-request]
+---
+# Expire stalled reservations
+
+The user approved a 30-minute reservation inactivity limit. READY reservations
+must not indefinitely exclude other eligible agents. ACTIVE tasks with valid
+leases remain protected; dependencies and capability tiers still apply.
+
+Reuse investigation: inspected Node, claim/_claim_locked, check_timeouts,
+structure add/split, event storage, replay and production-contract tests.
+The existing transaction lock, authenticated append-only event history,
+NODE_EDITED audit event, and fencing tokens already supply the required
+mechanisms. No browser write API or second coordination store is needed.
+No graph provider is available in this session; targeted source searches used.
+
+Use existing node creation and task lifecycle event timestamps to measure
+inactivity, including old reservations. Do not infer missing history or reset
+old deadlines on process restart. The clock starts at creation (including time
+waiting for dependencies); claim/renew/release/retry renew the inactivity anchor.
+Only READY reservations expire. A native task timeout makes its reservation
+eligible for immediate release. Missing age evidence fails visibly.
+
+Claim and check-timeouts expire reservations under the existing transaction
+lock. Expiry clears only reserved_for, records its old value and age evidence
+in NODE_EDITED, and leaves task identity, context, edges and tier intact.
+No forced takeover of an unexpired ACTIVE task and no automatic execution.
+
+The snapshot format and event names stay unchanged. Legacy workers can read
+released reservations, but must upgrade to run expiry themselves. Recovery
+and replay tools must upgrade before rebuilding logs containing reservation
+expiry metadata; old replay code ignores that metadata. The web remains a
+read-only observer and needs no credential expansion.
+
+## Verification before installation
+
+18 public-client regression cases pass using real file/Git stores, including
+boundary timing, active renewal, fencing, tier/dependency protection, two-worker
+contention, missing history, split children, replay and rejected Git publication.
+Three hand mutations (1801-second boundary, allowing ACTIVE reservation expiry,
+and dropping replay's release) each failed regression assertions and were restored.
+Source/test self-review checked the tracked tests scope and full branch diff.
+The full project preflight is the remaining release gate, not implied by these
+focused results. No other employee's runtime has been upgraded by this work.
+
+Live GUI state was inspected read-only: 72 COMPLETED and two READY tasks,
+cloud-media and cloud-image, both reserved for codex-cloud-music. Their latest
+release events were approximately 213 and 212 hours old. Cleanup will re-read
+state under the Git transaction lock and will not claim or execute those tasks.
